{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Fund optional gynaecological health consultations for girls aged 11-16",
        "additional_details": "Endometriosis, PCOS (PMOS), and fibroids affect millions of UK women. Endometriosis takes on average 9 years to diagnose and 39% of women visited their GP 10+ times before being taken seriously. There is peer-reviewed research that suggests endometriosis exhibits all 8 hallmarks of cancer, yet receives none of its screening urgency. A study suggests that women with endometriosis are 4x more likely to develop ovarian cancer. Undetected, these conditions can cause infertility, organ damage, and cost the UK \u00a38.2 billion annually. Early detection starts at puberty.",
        "background": "Fund and offer all girls in state and independent secondary schools in England: a pelvic ultrasound at start and end of secondary school (age 11\u201312 and 15\u201316), screening for endometriosis, PCOS (PMOS) and uterine fibroids, plus a confidential gynaecological specialist consultation.",
